# What stays on this machine and never goes to GitHub.
#
# Three reasons a file is here: it is rebuilt by a setup script, it is not ours
# to redistribute, or it records something about the person running her - what
# was said in the room, what is on the disk, which games are installed.

# --- Python environments --------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt by each Setup-*.cmd. They are also tied to the Python install and the
# folder path of the machine that made them, so a copied one does not work.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- The voice model ------------------------------------------------------
# tts\Setup-TTS.cmd downloads it from the glados-tts project. The weights are
# not covered by the MIT licence (see tts\NOTICE.txt), and two of the files are
# over GitHub's 100 MB limit anyway.
tts/models/
tts/models.zip

# --- Speech she has generated ---------------------------------------------
tts/cache/
tts/say.wav

# --- Settings and state she writes for herself ----------------------------
# config.json can hold an Anthropic API key in plain text. The defaults live in
# glados.ps1, so a missing file costs nothing.
config.json
config.json.bak*
games.json
brain/brain-config.json
brain/timers.json
brain/notes.json
brain/*.bak
voice/voice-config.json
voice/state.json
voice/followup.json
voice/glow.json
voice/*.lock
*.pid
*.tmp

# --- What she heard, saw and logged ---------------------------------------
voice/inbox/
voice/wake-audio/
voice/models/
eye/frames/
*.log

# --- Troubleshooting output -----------------------------------------------
# Hardware, user name and folder paths.
startup-error.txt
diagnose.txt
amsi-probe.txt
commit_probe.txt
probe/system-probe.txt

# --- Retired animation frames ---------------------------------------------
# install.ps1 moves superseded frames here; nothing loads them.
assets/old_frames/
